# Nested collection scans vs necessary sorts

A one-shot XML/clip export of a few hundred tags is I/O-bound. Still do not leave an inner loop that walks the **entire** session for every candidate when the inner loop only cares about a small subset.

- **Copy of the working vector is O(N) and required** when the pass mutates intervals or appends synthetics. Do not treat that copy as a defect.
- **`stable_sort` is the right tool** when storage order is not the emission comparator (TagSession sorts by `startMs`/`markMs`; export orders by `markMs`, non-Goal before Goal, then stamped `startMs`). A linear merge of “originals + synthetics” is only O(N) if both sides are already in that comparator. They are not.
- **Do collect the relevant subset once.** `hasExplicitGoalTagForTeam` only needs explicit Goal tags. Build that list (and cache association intervals) in one pass, then scan it per scored-follow-up candidate: O(N + C·G), not O(C·N) with interval math on every tag.
- **Running totals walk once.** If a later pass needs “score after every Goal through index i”, accumulate while emitting. Do not recount the prefix for each index.

```cpp
// BAD — every scored follow-up rescan the full session and recomputes Goal intervals
for (const auto& tag : tags) {
  if (!followUpPathContainsScoredGoal(tag.followUpEvent)) continue;
  if (hasExplicitGoalTagForTeam(tags, tag)) continue;  // walks all N tags
}

// BAD — “avoid sort” by merging lists that are not in emission order
// session order != exportTagComesBefore; interval stamp changes startMs

// GOOD — one pass over Goals, then candidates scan only that list; keep stable_sort
const QVector<ExplicitGoal> explicitGoals = collectExplicitGoals(tags);
for (const auto& tag : tags) {
  if (!followUpPathContainsScoredGoal(tag.followUpEvent)) continue;
  if (hasExplicitGoalTagForTeam(explicitGoals, tag)) continue;
}
std::stable_sort(expanded.begin(), expanded.end(), exportTagComesBefore);
```
